re", "chi2", "contingency test", "independence test"\n\nOPERATION SELECTION PRIORITY:\n\nSTEP 2A: Check for explicit statistical keywords\nIf query contains:\nANOVA, t-test, chi-square, correlation, regression, Tukey, post-hoc, p-value, effect size,\nstatistical testing, significantly differ, compare distributions, hypothesis test, differ significantly\n→ operation = "custom_transform"\n→ has_gap = true\n\nDETERMINE TEST TYPE (set in gap_reason):\n\n2-GROUP COMPARISON SIGNALS (use t-test, NOT ANOVA):\n- Query compares exactly 2 groups:\n  "Y versus others", "Y vs N", "between X and Y", "compared to", "versus others"\n  "differ between", "compare between two"\n- Binary column values: Y/N, True/False, 0/1\n→ gap_reason = "Two-group statistical comparison: use independent samples t-test (scipy.stats.ttest_ind) with normality check (Shapiro-Wilk). If non-normal, use Mann-Whitney U (scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu). Do NOT use ANOVA."\n\n3-OR-MORE GROUP COMPARISON SIGNALS (use ANOVA):\n- Query mentions 3+ categories, multiple groups, or uses "across groups/categories"\n- Explicit "ANOVA", "F-test", "Tukey", "post-hoc"\n→ gap_reason = "Multi-group statistical comparison: use one-way ANOVA (scipy.stats.f_oneway)."\n\nOTHER STATISTICAL TESTS:\n- Correlation → gap_reason = "Correlation analysis: use scipy.stats.pearsonr or spearmanr."\n- Regression → gap_reason = "Regression analysis: use scipy.stats.linregress or statsmodels OLS."\n- Chi-square → gap_reason = "Independence test: use scipy.stats.chi2_contingency."\n\nSTEP 2B: Check for variation/comparison patterns\nIf query contains:\n- "variation across", "variation by", "variations across"\n- "differences across", "differences by"\n- "compare across", "compare by"\n- "distribution across", "distribution by"\n→ operation = "groupby_aggregate"\n→ has_gap = false\n\nSTEP 2C: Detect basic operations\n- "filter", "where", "only", "exclude" → filter\n- "top N", "count by", "most common" → groupby_aggregate\n- "summary", "describe", "s